From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_GPU_PASS_TIME=1 (log only): after nx2:vi2's 600-present line, the frame times in 16.7 ms bins and Ocarina of Time's game speed (game seconds per second of the guest counter) from the dynamic-fps routine's two words (patch 0149, main+0x4E9FE00, address noted by the loader); unset: as before

T180p (writer P), part 2 of EDEN_UP_GPU_PASS_TIME=1 (the front's gpu_time_probe.inc has part 1).
Log only. After nx2:vi2's "last 600 presents" line, two more lines:
- "nx2:vi2 last 600 presents shape": the 599 frame times in 16.7 ms bins (<16.7, <33.3, <50,
  <66.7, <83.3, <100, >=100 ms).
- "nx2:vi2 last 600 presents game speed": with EDEN_NX2_OOT_DYNAMIC_FPS=1 (patch 0149) the loader
  notes where the routine keeps its two words (main+0x4E9FE00, from the routine's adrp/add:
  +0 the counter at its last call, +8 the smoothed frame time in counter ticks, capped at
  CNTFRQ/20 = 50 ms, smoothed by 1/8). Each present reads both; per routine call seen the game
  advances max(own step, smoothed) seconds (the routine takes the smoothed time when it is over
  1.03x the own step). Game speed = game seconds / seconds of the guest counter between the calls
  seen. The own step (s1/s0 of the game's state) is not read: taken as 1/30 s, which matters only
  for calls whose smoothed time is under 34.3 ms. Calls that fall between two presents with no
  present of their own are not seen (counted as "gaps that look like more than one call").
Cost with the switch: two 8-byte guest reads and a few additions per present. Unset: one test of a
static bool per present; nso.cpp's routine is unchanged (ApplyOcarinaDynamicFps only returns
whether it put the routine in). No shader, pipeline or translation file is touched: KEEPS THE STORE.
